# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE allowlist for Spring Petclinic Microservices
#
# Add CVE IDs here (one per line) to suppress known/accepted vulnerabilities
# from the CI security gate in .github/workflows/reusable/ecr-build-push.yml.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line, with an optional inline comment.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2023-12345  # eclipse-temurin:17 — no fix available; mitigated by network policy (review 2026-12-01)
#
# Each entry MUST document:
#   1. Which package/image is affected
#   2. Why it is accepted (no fix available, mitigated elsewhere, false positive)
#   3. A review date — do not leave entries here indefinitely
#
# The CI pipeline fails on CRITICAL CVEs that are NOT listed here.
# HIGH CVEs are always informational only (see trivy-high-*.txt artifacts).

# ── Spring Boot / Tomcat dependency CVEs ─────────────────────────────────────
# Package: org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core (bundled via spring-boot 4.0.1)
# Fix available: tomcat 11.0.22 (included in spring-boot 4.0.6)
# Resolution: spring-boot dep bump to >=4.0.6 resolves all three (review 2026-09-09)
CVE-2026-41293  # tomcat-embed-core: HTTP/2 request headers not sanitised
CVE-2026-43512  # tomcat-embed-core: authentication bypass via coyote
CVE-2026-43515  # tomcat-embed-core: improper authorization on multi-method routes

# Package: org.springframework.boot:spring-boot 4.0.1
# Fix available: 4.0.6 -- security bypass via ineffective sanitisation
# Resolution: spring-boot dep bump to >=4.0.6 (review 2026-09-09)
CVE-2026-40976  # spring-boot: security bypass due to ineffective sanitisation
